<p> I Robot, directed by Alex Proyas is a film about future robots being used in our everyday lives as helpers for people to perform tasks. The robots are programmed to adhere to the Three Laws of Robotics which means they cannot harm or endanger life in anyway, but when a scientist is murdered and Detective Spooner investigates, he starts questioning the harmlessness of robots and if they are truly safe. The portrayal of artificial intelligence in movies such as I Robot affects the way that society views real-world applications of AI technologies and the potential impacts they could have on society as they become more prevalent in the future. </p>
<br>
<p> VIKI is the main AI in "I Robot." She oversees the drones and the building’s security. VIKI is also like a super-intelligent surveillance system. She can analyze and interpret video, as well as interact with spoken language, and she uses these abilities to create a unique answer and action for each situation instead of just following a script. And she can also control the security of the building by way of locking all the doors, placing the whole building in lockdown, etc. All this shows her ability to make advanced decisions and to control systems. Although, of course, what VIKI can do is far beyond what today’s AIs are capable of, she does represent the danger of giving one machine, without human oversight, too much power. </p>

